Problem on Averages-12 - Placement Exercise
NOTE: This kind of question is very common in campus placement ( TCS, Wipro, etc.) because it makes the use of average and some basic logic.

Problem:
The average score of a batsman in 8 innings is 42 runs. 
In the 9th inning, he scores 78 runs, which increases his average by 4 runs. 
Find his new average after the 9th inning.

Solution:
Note: Formula of Average = Sum of observations / No. of observations.
Sum of observations = Averages X No. of observations.

Original average of batsman = 42 runs

Number of innings = 8

Original total score = 8 × 42 = 336 runs

Score in 9th inning = 78 runs

New total score = Original total score + Score in 9th inning
New total score = 336 + 78 = 414 runs

New number of innings = 9

New average = 414 ÷ 9 = 46 runs

Increase in average = 46 - 42 = 4 runs ✅

Final Answer
👍 New average of the batsman after the 9th inning = 46 runs
